# Database needs confirmation

Local dev uses the production Neon database. A write from this machine changes live Cubity data.

Never change database data or schema unless the user clearly agreed **in the current message**.

## Counts as a change

- `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`, `TRUNCATE`, or any Prisma write (`create`, `update`, `delete`, `upsert`, `updateMany`, `deleteMany`)
- `prisma migrate`, `prisma db push`, `prisma db execute`, or SQL that alters tables
- Seed scripts, one-off scripts, or server actions that write clients, dues, payments, or payment settings
- Editing rows in Prisma Studio or any database GUI

## Still allowed without asking

- Reading data (`findMany`, `SELECT`, opening a screen)
- Editing application code that would write later, without running that write
- `prisma generate`

## Confirmation required

Treat these as permission: "yes, change the database", "add this client", "run the migration", "delete that row".

If they only say "fix the screen", "looks good", or "commit", **ask first**. Do not infer yes.

Stop and ask: "This writes to the live database. Should I go ahead?"
